+// Build switch, default 0 (= the lock's code): large (2 MB) pages for the engine's big
+// tables when the process can enable SeLockMemoryPrivilege; on any failure the lock's
+// allocation is used, silently. 1 = the transposition table's clusters; 2 = also the
+// network's first-layer weights and one block per search worker for its six history /
+// correction tables. Same sizes, same zeroed contents, same indexing: only the page size
